<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 30 September, from 420 to 1955.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/jerome" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jerome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/420">420 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,606 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">St Jerome dies in Bethlehem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerome">Jerome</a> died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bethlehem">Bethlehem</a>, where he had translated most of the Bible into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> and Greek. His Vulgate became the standard Bible of the Western Church for over a thousand years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">489 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,537 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodoric the Great defeats Odoacer at the Battle of Verona</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a>, leading his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> in person, won a decisive victory at Verona over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, who fled to Ravenna. Theodoric was then free to take Pavia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, and by 493 he ruled Italy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/737">737 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,289 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Türgesh tribesmen capture the baggage train of an Umayyad army</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Retreating across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Oxus</a> from Khuttal, the Umayyad army of Asad ibn Abdallah al-Qasri lost its baggage train, sent ahead, to the pursuing Türgesh. The failed campaign ended Arab control of the upper Oxus valley and opened Khurasan to the Türgesh.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-transoxiana">Muslim conquest of Transoxiana</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1139">1139 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">887 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A great earthquake strikes the Caucasus near Ganja</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">One of the worst earthquakes in history struck around Ganja, in lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. Its disputed death toll of 230,000 to 300,000 makes it one of the deadliest earthquakes ever recorded.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganja-azerbaijan">Ganja, Azerbaijan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1342 CE <span class="tih-ago">684 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An Anglo-Breton army defeats a larger Franco-Breton force at Morlaix</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Lanmeur in Brittany, an Anglo-Breton army defeated a far larger Franco-Breton force in the first land battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> had sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-montfort">John of Montfort</a> in the Breton Civil War, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-of-blois">Charles of Blois</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1399">1399 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">627 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parliament accepts Richard II's deposition and Henry IV's claim</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard II's abdication was read to an assembly at Westminster, which then acclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-england">Henry Bolingbroke</a> as Henry IV. The Lancastrian usurpation sowed the seeds of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mozart's The Magic Flute premieres in Vienna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Die Zauberflöte opened at the Theater auf der Wieden with Mozart conducting. It was a popular success, and he died nine weeks later at the age of 35.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1938">1938 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chamberlain returns from Munich promising 'peace for our time'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Neville Chamberlain landed at Heston waving the declaration signed with Hitler and later spoke of 'peace for our time'. Within six months <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> had seized the rest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1955">1955 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">71 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Dean dies in a car crash aged 24</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Actor James Dean was killed when his Porsche collided with another car in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. Two of his three starring films were released after his death, making him a lasting icon of youth.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 30 September <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rumi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rumi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rumi</span><span class="tp">1207–1273</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-morelos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-maria-morelos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José María Morelos</span><span class="tp">1765–1815</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 30 September <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-ii-of-vladimir"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yaroslav-ii-of-vladimir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Yaroslav II of Vladimir</span><span class="tp">1191–1246</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-black"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leszek-the-black.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leszek the Black</span><span class="tp">c. 1241–1288</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/reginald-grey-3rd-baron-grey-de-ruthyn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/reginald-grey-3rd-baron-grey-de-ruthyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Reginald Grey, 3rd Baron Grey de Ruthyn</span><span class="tp">c. 1362–1440</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ouchi-yoshitaka"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ouchi-yoshitaka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ōuchi Yoshitaka</span><span class="tp">1507–1551</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/patrick-white"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/patrick-white.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Patrick White</span><span class="tp">1912–1990</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
